  known_gap the Python peer's witness for this organ no longer exists on disk; the entry named a file that could not be opened, which is the one thing a witness must never be. The line is removed rather than repointed, and the live evidence for this architecture is what remains listed.
architecture discipl-composition
  canonical_name DisCIPLCompositionGraph
  consumes CommandAdvertisement
  family capability
  domain Capability / Composition
  layer capability/composition
  semantic_question What typed chain of transforms bridges this source family to this destination family, and at what cost?
  purpose The native composition calculus: contracts with success_prior, transform_cost, semantic_loss. Never reimplemented in Python -- the engine is called.
  maturity implemented
  node_types ContractRow
  node_types Family
  edge_types transforms
  edge_types bridges
  forbidden_inference a proposed chain -> a runnable chain (binding is separate)
  computational_form fused
  command BonfyreDiscipl
  source_path lib/libbonfyre/src/bf_discipl.c
  source_path cmd/BonfyreDiscipl/src/main.c
  witness cmd/BonfyreDiscipl/tests/composition_test.sh
  source_lineage capability closure essay
  interacts command-law-seeds-discipl
  interacts estate-bridges-into-discipl
  node_types PhenotypeFamily
  node_types CarrierFamily
  node_types RetainedBody
  edge_types retained_as
  edge_types conforms_to
  edge_types ingested_as
  edge_types emits_kind
  forbidden_inference a seeded edge -> an executed transform; nothing in the lattice has run a binary
  forbidden_inference a carrier family -> every retained body being that carrier; the edge carries the rate, not a certainty
  forbidden_inference the estate-wide retention rate -> a per-phenotype rate
  invariant a prior on the estate bridge is measured or the edge is refused; bf_discipl_seed_estate_bridge returns 2 rather than substituting a default. The measured rate is 0.513 -- 2,505 of 4,885 occurrences have a body on disk now -- and is per occurrence, because the lattice starts from an occurrence and not from a fetch
  invariant the carrier edge is conditional on the phenotype that declares the carrier, never on the retained body. Seeded from the body it made all fifteen phenotypes equivalent; conditional, EVENT reaches RSS at 0.990 and SERVICE_CAPABILITY reaches OpenAPI at 0.012 and thirteen phenotypes reach no carrier at all
  invariant a carrier with no observed population gets no family; a probe that has never fired contributes nothing. Three of the nine detectable carriers have one: RSS at 474 occurrences, Atom at 26, OpenAPI at 19
  internal_calculus bounded enumeration of simple paths to --depth, ranked by the unfloored confidence product less drift less amortised cost
  internal_calculus modality transition loss: an edge whose command carries material into a different modality loses 0.15, one that does not loses 0.03
  internal_calculus execution: a proposed chain is walked hop by hop with the real binaries, each hop's output taken from the manifest that binary writes rather than from a filename guess, and a declared carrier passed down to the command that can use it
  invariant a hop's output is what the binary declared it produced. A binary that exits zero and leaves no declared output fails the hop; its stdout is never passed to the next command as if it were material
  invariant an invocation is bound only after it ran and left something on disk; exit zero alone binds nothing
  invariant a call whose usage names a database, a URL, a model or a key is never probed. Finding out how to call it would mean writing to real state or touching the network, and an unbound command is a smaller cost than either
  invariant a command with no checked argv stops the walk and is named. An invocation is bound only after it has been run and its output looked at -- four of twenty-seven are, and a guessed argv that exits zero would let a receipt claim a hop ran when nothing happened
  known_gap the lattice contracted 104 edges and had executed none of them, which made every score a claim about a claim. Chains now run end to end on retained bodies -- carrier RSS, ingest to normalized text, hash to digest -- and invocations are no longer checked one at a time by hand: `bind-commands` reads each binary's own usage, derives the file-in calls it claims to accept, and binds one only after running it and finding something on disk that was not there before. Seven of twenty-seven are bound that way; 12 offer no call that takes a file without also naming a database, a URL, a model or a key, and 4 print no usage block at all.
  known_gap binding by execution proves a call works and cannot prove it is the right call. The prober demonstrated this on itself: offered every safe shape bonfyre-tag accepts, it bound `detect-lang`, which exits zero and writes a file and is not what Tag declares it makes -- `predict` needs a trained model and is refused as unsafe to probe. Shapes are now tried in the order of what the command declares it produces and every binding reports whether the call it found names a declared output. T_TAG's says false.
  known_gap the first runner hardcoded ingest's output as normalized.txt and fell back to the hop's stdout when that was missing. On a body with no extension ingest detected `unknown`, wrote the file under its original name, and the chain carried ingest's own log into the hash. Both hops reported ok and the composition was wrong -- exit zero is not review, and a silent fallback is how a wrong answer gets a receipt.
  known_gap a carrier measured on the bytes did not reach the command that could use it: a walk starting at T_CARRIER_RSS told ingest nothing and ingest detected `unknown` on a feed the estate had already proven was a feed. The start family is now read as well as the hop destinations.
  known_gap the two witnesses this entry carried were both .py.archive -- archived files that cannot run. It held `implemented` on evidence that had been deleted, which is the laundering the atlas forbids one level in: the maturity was checked once and the witness was retired without the claim being revisited. A live witness now stands in their place.
  known_gap the engine honoured --depth only to 2. It searched for a direct edge, then for one intermediate, then reported candidate_chains: [] -- an authoritative negative about paths held in its own table. T_WORKFLOW_STAGE -> T_QUEUE_JOB -> T_EXECUTION -> T_LEDGER_EVENT -> T_VALUE_CAPTURE is four contracted edges and was reported unreachable at --depth 6. The emptiness of discipl_chains was never about the chains.
  known_gap every proposal was keyed discipl_chain:discipl-proposal, so each one replaced the last and the table could not accumulate more than one row per verb. Chains are now identified by the families they walk.
  known_gap the reach difference between phenotypes was an evidence gap until conformance was run on every receipt. It is now a coverage fact with a measured floor: across all 3,316 receipts, 523 bodies conform, 2 carry a carrier no phenotype declares, 1,964 carry nothing the nine probes can detect, and 325 name a body this estate no longer holds. Running it everywhere added four conformances. The thirteen phenotypes that reach fewer terminals do so because their bytes carry no detectable carrier, not because nobody looked -- but `no_carrier_detected` still means nine needles found nothing, never that the body carries none.
  known_gap the conformance compiler had only a single-receipt entry point, so sweeping the estate meant parsing 4,891 occurrences once per receipt. The evidence gap was a cost of the interface, not a decision about the sources; a batch mode that parses the corpus once closed it in one run.
  known_gap carrier detection returned the same value for a body that matched no probe and a body that is not on disk. A sweep reporting both as nothing-detected reports an absence of evidence as evidence of absence, about 325 receipts whose bytes this estate has lost. They are separate outcomes now.
  invariant a chain that leaves a modality and returns to it is neither proposed nor stored when a shorter chain to the same goal passes through the same families in the same order without that trip, at no greater cost or loss; it is listed under refused_detours with the chain that covers it
  invariant a round trip that is the only route stays proposed, and a longer chain that changes what a later step receives is a different output and is not a detour
  witness cmd/BonfyreDiscipl/tests/composition_test.sh proves TranscriptClean -> Brief -> Narrate -> Transcribe -> Segment is refused as covered by the one-hop chain and not stored, that Brief -> Narrate -> Transcribe -> Segment stays because nothing shorter exists, and that the longer chain through TranscriptClean is kept as a different output
  forbidden_inference a chain not refused as a detour -> a useful chain; only a modality round trip covered by a shorter chain is refused
  known_gap the search still finds compositions that are legal and worthless when they are not a covered round trip. A speak-then-listen chain with no shorter alternative is proposed, ranked last by modality loss; conversion cost is a declared prior, not a measured time or energy, and nothing asks whether the output serves the consumer that requested it.
  known_gap the bridge emits `rows_claiming_a_body` for rows carrying body_path and body_bytes. That is the right denominator for "can I hand bytes to a binary" and it is not a count of retention claims, which is a different and much more honest number. The two were briefly reported as one.
  known_gap counting observation rows instead of occurrences inflated the bridge prior from 0.513 to 0.691. An occurrence observed twice contributes twice, and "did this fetch work" is not the question a chain rooted at a phenotype asks. Both rates are now emitted so the difference stays visible rather than being quietly chosen.
  known_gap the `source_retained` rung was awarded for the presence of a `body_path` field rather than for a body, and nothing re-checked it after the writer set it. Verified against the filesystem it costs 3 rows of 2,885 -- the rung was substantially honest and is now checked rather than believed. An earlier note here read the 691 rows that name a body whose bytes are gone as 691 false retention claims; every one of those is a `boundary_response`, a lower rung that never claimed retention, and the stronger number was mine from conflating "names a body" with "claims the rung".
  known_gap 451 occurrences name a boundary-response body this estate no longer holds. Recovering them means re-fetching 451 external hosts, which is an outward act rather than a repair, so the claim is checked and left standing at the rung it actually earned.
  known_gap the 17 terminal families a retained body cannot reach are not one gap but two: 13 are model-internal and need weights rather than documents, which is correct and permanent; 4 root in capability, telemetry, alert and graph, which are real roots this bridge simply does not touch.
  interacts discipl-asks-the-pure-tier
  witness architecture/tests/chain_portfolio_test.sh
  known_gap the engine ranked chains and could not answer which combinations of them fit a budget, which is the question an operator actually has: nobody runs one chain. That is a subset-sum over accumulated cost, and it is now stated as a pure job rather than answered here, so the tier decides where it may be computed and a second reducer checks the answer.
  known_gap the engine's scores had no second opinion until now. Agreement between the interaction net and enumeration says the search is computed consistently; it says nothing about the declared priors both were handed, which remain unmeasured.

